      "writtenOn": "2020-03-05T03:05:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The logic here is that\nIf the loop ends and the listener has not set the exit code yet then it means something goes wrong. We should return `status`.\nIf the loop ends and the listener has set the exit code, the status will always be non zero (broken pipe? i guess). We should return the exit code instead of `status`.\n\nMaybe it is better to name `getExitCode` `getExitCodeOrElse`?",
